============================================================================================
PART 1 -- the three algebras: number of components, component degrees
============================================================================================
Each table row uses the algebra of p.21 (q=4), Example 2 (q=9) or Example 3
(q=25).  Both defining polynomials are quadratic, so dim_Fq A = 4 always.
The component degrees |S(nu)| are the sizes of the Galois orbits of the
root pairs (nu_1,nu_2);  this is computed explicitly, not assumed.

q = 4   F_4 = F_2[z]/(1 + 1x^1 + 1x^2)   (w = z = element 2; the two roots of the modulus are (2, 3))
   t1 = 2 + 1x^1 + 1x^2   t2 = 2 + 2x^1 + 1x^2
   square-free: t1 True, t2 True
   roots of t1 in F_16: [(0, 1), (1, 1)]   -> irreducible over F_q
   roots of t2 in F_16: [(1, 2), (3, 2)]   -> irreducible over F_q
   Galois orbits on root pairs: 2  of sizes [2, 2]
   => N = number of components = 2;  component degrees |S(nu)| = [2, 2]
   => dim_Fq A = sum_S |S(nu)| = 4   (= prod deg t_i = 4):  CONSISTENT

q = 9   F_9 = F_3[z]/(2 + 2x^1 + 1x^2)   (w = z = element 3; the two roots of the modulus are (3, 7))
   t1 = 3 + 1x^1 + 1x^2   t2 = 2 + 6x^1 + 1x^2
   square-free: t1 True, t2 True
   roots of t1 in F_81: [(1, 5), (1, 7)]   -> irreducible over F_q
   roots of t2 in F_81: [(6, 3), (6, 6)]   -> irreducible over F_q
   Galois orbits on root pairs: 2  of sizes [2, 2]
   => N = number of components = 2;  component degrees |S(nu)| = [2, 2]
   => dim_Fq A = sum_S |S(nu)| = 4   (= prod deg t_i = 4):  CONSISTENT

q = 25   F_25 = F_5[z]/(2 + 4x^1 + 1x^2)   (w = z = element 5; the two roots of the modulus are (5, 21))
   t1 = 20 + 1x^1 + 1x^2   t2 = 1 + 23x^1 + 1x^2
   square-free: t1 True, t2 True
   roots of t1 in F_625: [(2, 8), (2, 22)]   -> irreducible over F_q
   roots of t2 in F_625: [(14, 0), (23, 0)]   -> splits over F_q
   Galois orbits on root pairs: 2  of sizes [2, 2]
   => N = number of components = 2;  component degrees |S(nu)| = [2, 2]
   => dim_Fq A = sum_S |S(nu)| = 4   (= prod deg t_i = 4):  CONSISTENT

