============================================================================================
PART 2b -- the numbers themselves: does g_S divide x^n - lambda_S ?
============================================================================================
This is the decisive test of the transcription.  Each row says that g_S
generates a lambda_S-constacyclic code, so g_S must divide x^n - lambda_S
in F_q[x].  The test is run for EVERY admissible naming of omega, i.e. for
each choice of omega as one of the two roots of its defining quadratic
((2, 3) for F_4, (3, 7) for F_9, (5, 21) for F_25): 2*2*2 = 8
combinations, which is the complete set, not a sample.

  omega = (2, 3, 5):  13/13 rows divisible   ALL
  omega = (2, 3, 21):  13/13 rows divisible   ALL
  omega = (2, 7, 5):  13/13 rows divisible   ALL
  omega = (2, 7, 21):  13/13 rows divisible   ALL
  omega = (3, 3, 5):  13/13 rows divisible   ALL
  omega = (3, 3, 21):  13/13 rows divisible   ALL
  omega = (3, 7, 5):  13/13 rows divisible   ALL
  omega = (3, 7, 21):  13/13 rows divisible   ALL

  => transcription VALIDATED under every naming
     (13/13 in all 8 namings; the structured table agrees with the PDF, and
      the two independent transcriptions of Part 2 agree with each other)

